{
  "about": "Layer composition through the public check (LAYER-4, LAYER-8, LAYER-9, LAYER-12, SCHEMA-12, SCHEMA-13, FILE-5, P-CLR-2, P-NULL-1). YAML null outside a value or expression field is invalid_field_type in the layer that writes it. A member of columns, intermediates or rows written without the name or id composition matches it by misses it where it is written, named by its index, in an entry as in a child layer. Each clear entry that names what its layer cannot clear (nothing it inherits, a required or identity field, yamaa, type, a keyed member, an operation keyword without its field, a value that came from a schema default, or anything in a layer without a parent) fails as invalid_clear at its own clear[i], with the field the path ends at, and a valid entry beside them is not reported; a path outside the spec path notation, or beside one of its prefixes, fails when its layer is admitted. A finding names row templates and intermediates by id; requiredness applies to the pruned resolved specification, so an unread incomplete intermediate is pruned with its fault and a read one reports it; an input that only an unread lookup reads is pruned with its missing path, so a parent can leave an optional source for its children to supply, and an unread lookup without key, kept only to reach its refusal (LOOKUP-3), keeps no input live, so its refusal is what fails. A fragment's clear that names nothing the layers before it compose fails in the fragment. An include entry written as a URI is refused, and include written as one path is not a list. A child's definition of an inherited window merges with it by name, so VISITS orders the missing SEQ first and its rows run b, a, c: a reads b's VAL and c reads a's, while OTHER still numbers the rows by VAL. A resolved specification to which no layer contributes output misses it at the root. The converted negative-property-clear, as the converter wrote it, fails at the clear entry its 0.5 null became. Moved from declaration_layer_composition.rs at 55276b420, whose tests prepared the entry through prepare_specification with a test resolver and compared each finding's condition code, spec path and context, the layer the refusal named, or the code and path alone, and saved out.csv for the window; each case here is the public check, or the save, of the staged study. A row's phase, condition and rule are its condition code's registry entry. A finding in a layer also names that layer as source and the entry file as entry; a finding in the resolved specification names neither. The specifications are the tests' BASE, ENTRY, ROWS and WINDOWED and their edits. No engine output supplied these values.",
  "documents": {
    "base": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ninput:\n  DS: {path: ds.csv, types: {CODE: str}}\ncolumns:\n  - name: CODE\n    type: str\n    label: Code\n    derivation: DS.CODE\n    metadata: {origin: collected, owner: base}\n  - name: REASON\n    type: str\n    label: Reason\n    derivation:\n      mapping:\n        source: DS.CODE\n        dict: {AE: ADVERSE EVENT, PD: PROGRESSIVE DISEASE, 'NOT DONE': NOT DONE}\n        unmapped: OTHER\nmetadata: {scope: organization, owner: base}\n",
    "entry": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\nparent: base.yaml\ndomain: TEST\nkeys: [CODE]\noutput: {path: out.csv, columns: [CODE, REASON]}\n",
    "alone": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\nkeys: [ID]\ninput: {SRC: input.csv}\noutput: {path: output.csv, columns: [ID]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: int, label: Identifier, derivation: SRC.ID}\n",
    "keyed": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\nkeys: [ID]\ninput: {SRC: input.csv}\noutput: {path: output.csv, columns: [ID]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: str, label: Identifier, derivation: SRC.ID}\n",
    "rows": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: TEST\nkeys: [ID]\ninput: {SRC: {path: input.csv, key: [ID]}}\noutput: {path: output.csv, columns: [ID]}\nintermediates:\n  - {id: FIRST, dataset: SRC, key: [ID], other: 1}\nrows:\n  - {id: week2, dataset: SRC, other: 1}\n  - {id: 'week 3', dataset: SRC, other: 1}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: int, derivation: SRC.ID}\n",
    "windowed": "yamaa: \"1.0\"\ntype: spec\ndomain: OUT\nkeys: [ID]\ninput: {SRC: {path: input.csv, types: {SEQ: int, VAL: int}}}\nwindows:\n  VISITS: {group_by: [G], order_by: [SEQ]}\n  OTHER: {group_by: [G], order_by: [VAL]}\ncolumns:\n  - {name: ID, type: str, derivation: SRC.ID}\n  - {name: G, type: str, derivation: SRC.G}\n  - {name: SEQ, type: int, derivation: SRC.SEQ}\n  - {name: VAL, type: int, derivation: SRC.VAL}\n  - {name: PREV, type: int, derivation: {row_value: {source: VAL, offset: -1, window: VISITS}}}\n  - {name: RANK, type: int, derivation: {row_number: {window: OTHER}}}\noutput: {path: out.csv, columns: [ID, PREV, RANK]}\n"
  },
